<title>HONG KONG: Shanghai Hai Xing slides into red in H1.</title>
<headline>Shanghai Hai Xing slides into red in H1.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1996-08-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months ended June 30</p>
<p>(in million yuan unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (Chinese cents)	3.4 loss   vs 2.0 gain</p>
<p>    Dividend (Chinese cents) nil	  vs nil</p>
<p>    Exceptional items	  17.53	vs 72.16</p>
<p>    Net			    84.49 loss vs 50.51 gain</p>
<p>    Turnover		     1,648.53   vs 1,406.49</p>
<p>    Company name		 Shanghai Hai Xing Shipping Co Ltd</p>
<p>    Books close		  N/A</p>
<p>    Dividend payable	   N/A</p>
<p>NOTE - Shanghai Hai Xing is a Chinese shipping company.</p>
<p>Net is after exceptional gains on disposal of vessels.</p>
<p>The company said its earnings were hit by sluggish demand for domestic shipping services and higher finance costs.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6368</p>
</text>
